            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0212" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v5/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 71.</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Edward Everett to Mr.
                        Campbell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boston</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1858-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            29, 1858.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As the radical principle of the boundary is the forty-ninth degree of latitude,
                    and the only reason for departing from it was to give the whole of Vancouver’s
                    Island to the party acquiring the largest part of it, the deflection from the
                    forty-ninth degree southward should be limited to that object, and the nearest
                    channel adopted which fulfills the above conditions.<seg type="margin">Mr.
                        Everett on the channel of the treaty.</seg></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWARD EVERETT.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Archibald Campbell</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
